WEBVTT

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:12.179
[♪♪♪]

00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:38.121
NARRATOR: Once upon a time, on a beautiful country day,

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:42.041
the birds weren't singing, the fish weren't jumping,

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:46.213
and there was not a hopping rabbit to be found,

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:47.923
for everyone was gathered

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:50.551
to celebrate two very special people

00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:55.848
at what can only be described as a storybook wedding.

00:00:55.848 --> 00:00:58.392
[WAGNER'S "BRIDAL CHORUS" PLAYING]

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:03.647
[BOTH SIGH]

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:05.065
[GUESTS MURMURING]

00:01:07.026 --> 00:01:08.360
Aw.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.361
[SNIFFLING]

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:10.445
I promised myself

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:11.822
I wouldn't cry.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:14.282
Well, that was dumb.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.619
[WOMEN SIGHING]

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:18.704
Hello.

00:01:21.665 --> 00:01:25.210
Aw. Ah. Ah!

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:28.630
Hi. Heh.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.257
Hello.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.803
Welcome, friends. We are gathered here today

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:37.890
to join Bea and Thomas in holy matrimony.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.892
You're taking this so well.

00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:41.936
He's a good man. Makes her happy.

00:01:41.936 --> 00:01:44.145
And also a special day for their family,

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.856
the beloved rabbits.

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:47.983
Your former enemy is here to stay.

00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:49.526
We found common ground.

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:51.111
He's about to be our guardian.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.572
Nah, this is just a little something between them.

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:56.909
The old you would have gone bonkers-berserk by now.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:59.787
I've changed, cousin. ...welcoming a new parent.

00:01:59.787 --> 00:02:02.998
A loaded hand grenade, just waiting to explode.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:05.417
Not anymore. A father, if you will.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:07.210
Father? [CLICKS]

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.253
Father.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:09.254
[WHISTLING]

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.631
You're not my father!

00:02:10.631 --> 00:02:11.590
[MIMICS EXPLOSION]

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.342
[GRUNTING] [GUESTS GASPING]

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:16.929
[RABBITS GRUNTING] [GROWLS]

00:02:16.929 --> 00:02:19.139
[GROANING]

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.141
[GUESTS SCREAMING]

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.937
♪ Lying there in the sun All things to everyone ♪

00:02:24.937 --> 00:02:26.271
♪ Run, run away ♪

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:27.272
[SNORTING]

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:29.441
[YELLS]

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:32.111
[GUESTS CLAMORING]

00:02:32.111 --> 00:02:33.821
♪ Run, run away, hey! ♪

00:02:33.821 --> 00:02:35.739
♪ If you're in the swing ♪

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:38.993
[GRUNTS] [GROANS]

00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:42.496
Hm. Aah! Aah! Ah!

00:02:42.496 --> 00:02:45.165
[SCREAMING] [GUESTS GASPING]

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.002
You'll never be my father!

00:02:48.002 --> 00:02:50.629
And everyone can see your underpants!

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:53.841
Hm. BENJAMIN: Peter. Peter.

00:02:53.841 --> 00:02:55.174
Peter.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.260
Peter, the ring. Wha...?

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.470
[MUSIC SLOWS TO A STOP]

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:01.890
Right, right.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.143
Where'd I put...? Did I...?

00:03:04.143 --> 00:03:05.978
Was it...? No, was it...?

00:03:05.978 --> 00:03:08.313
Hang on. I had it in the...

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:09.481
Ah!

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:13.986
[CHUCKLES]

00:03:13.986 --> 00:03:16.030
It's always in the last place you look.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.906
You only have two pockets.

00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:19.950
You may now kiss the groom.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.910
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:25.039
[GUESTS CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:27.124
[SIGHS] [SNIFFLING, SOBBING]

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:28.876
Huh?

00:03:28.876 --> 00:03:29.918
What?

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:33.047
[BEA & THOMAS CHUCKLING]

00:03:33.047 --> 00:03:34.506
♪ Ooh, yeah... ♪

00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:36.008
[GUESTS CHEERING]

00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:37.509
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:41.013
BEA & THOMAS: Bye!

00:03:41.013 --> 00:03:42.139
Bye!

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:43.807
Bye. We'll miss you.

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:46.185
♪ Oh, oh She's not there no more... ♪

00:03:46.185 --> 00:03:48.896
NARRATOR: So Bea and Mr. McGregor were married,

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.065
and off they went on their honeymoon.

00:03:51.065 --> 00:03:54.484
Things couldn't have been more peaceful in Windermere

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.695
until, sometime later...

00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:58.947
[BABY CRYING]

00:03:58.947 --> 00:04:00.365
You just take this out.

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:01.408
[DOLL CRYING]

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:02.450
You see?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.578
Now you try.

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:08.331
Dad, it's Peter Rabbit from the book.

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:12.419
Oh, I hate that I'm the face of this.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:15.923
But every story can only have one good guy, so...

00:04:15.923 --> 00:04:18.550
Peter doesn't have a dad. He got put in a pie.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.844
That's why he's so naughty. What?

00:04:20.844 --> 00:04:23.138
And there's Flopsy, Mopsy and Cotton-Tail.

00:04:23.138 --> 00:04:25.390
I'm Flopsy. And I'm Mopsy.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.684
And I'm the hero. But I'm not naughty.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:31.146
Did this kid even read the book? Did you read the book?

00:04:31.146 --> 00:04:33.774
I am so busy. Ah.

00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:35.234
I'm saving it for summer.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:37.694
Are you the author? I'm still getting used

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:38.987
to people calling me that.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.948
It's really the rabbits' story.

00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:42.407
I just wrote it down.

00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:44.993
This is my husband. He's our publisher.

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:46.411
I wouldn't say "publisher."

00:04:46.411 --> 00:04:49.539
I just, uh... I just do the typesetting,

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.959
turned our dining room into a printing workshop,

00:04:51.959 --> 00:04:54.419
created the lithography with a five-color palette

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:56.755
for the illustrations, apart from ones of the garden,

00:04:56.755 --> 00:05:00.300
which call for more green. Don't reveal all your secrets.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.344
Well, it's wonderful. You paint the rabbits with such love.

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:06.223
Well, it comes naturally. It's our family.

00:05:06.223 --> 00:05:07.599
Thanks for your contribution.

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:09.184
It goes directly to preserving their land.

00:05:09.184 --> 00:05:10.769
Thank you. Bye.

00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:12.104
Bye.

00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:13.063
[KNOCKING]

00:05:13.063 --> 00:05:14.606
MOIRA: Afternoon!

00:05:14.606 --> 00:05:15.857
Congratulations, you two.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:18.068
Thanks, Moira. Oh, the mail.

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.736
Choose to see who gets it.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:22.906
Chest. Toe. Chest.

00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.491
Ears. Tail.

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:26.451
Oh! Yes!

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:28.620
How does he always win?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.580
Because he invented the game.

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:36.377
Peter? Is that you? Johnny?

00:05:36.377 --> 00:05:38.088
What are you doing out of London?

00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:40.299
We're up here doing some cheese tasting.

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:41.300
[SNIFFS]

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.467
Heard about the wedding.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.303
Any babies yet? Only been a month.

00:05:44.303 --> 00:05:47.472
Oh, the wife and I have had 15 kids in that time.

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:49.516
This is the first day away from them,

00:05:49.516 --> 00:05:51.601
and, oh, the peace and quiet.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.562
But I'd be lying if I said we didn't miss them terribly

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:56.023
and they're all we talk about.

00:05:56.023 --> 00:05:57.983
Aw, cute.

00:05:57.983 --> 00:06:00.401
But there's no babies. We're their family.

00:06:00.401 --> 00:06:03.113
Until you're not.

00:06:03.113 --> 00:06:06.074
Ah! Congratulations on the book, by the way.

00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:07.909
My kids absolutely loved it.

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:09.536
Oh, it's not about me.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:11.370
It's just great that kids get to read

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.333
about positive role models like me.

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:15.500
[GRUNTS]

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.376
Peter! Ah!

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.962
[GASPS, GRUNTS]

00:06:18.962 --> 00:06:20.421
Oh, dear. My cheese.

00:06:20.421 --> 00:06:22.007
Well, good luck.

00:06:22.007 --> 00:06:24.343
BEA: I'm sure it was just an accident.

00:06:24.343 --> 00:06:26.678
It's not an accident.

00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:28.513
It's what he does.

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:29.764
He never behaves.

00:06:29.764 --> 00:06:31.808
He loves you. Don't listen to him.

00:06:31.808 --> 00:06:34.144
He doesn't listen to me. That's the problem.

00:06:34.144 --> 00:06:35.645
[WHISPERING] Not in front of him.

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:38.273
He can't understand me. Can he?

00:06:38.273 --> 00:06:39.858
No, but still, just...

00:06:39.858 --> 00:06:41.568
So if he can't understand me,

00:06:41.568 --> 00:06:44.112
why can't I say whatever it is that I want to say?

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:46.031
[WHISPERED OVERLAPPING ARGUING]

00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:47.199
Just say something nice.

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:49.201
Say something nice. Now! Go! Say it!

00:06:49.201 --> 00:06:51.119
I'm terribly sorry. Out loud!

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.454
[NORMALLY] I'm sorry, Peter. I love you,

00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:55.456
in the way that an adult human loves a--

00:06:55.456 --> 00:06:58.919
An animal rabbit. Thank you.

